# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# cs runtime state (never commit — it references local session ids)
.cs-last-index
.cs-ignore

# Local working notes. docs/HANDOVER.md is the published handover and stays
# public-safe; anything that has to name a real path, a real session or a
# local backup goes in a *.local.md beside it and is never committed.
*.local.md

# OS
.DS_Store

# Local task-tracking tooling. Beads (bd) is a personal workflow choice, not a
# requirement for working on cs — the issue tracker for this project is GitHub
# Issues, and CONTRIBUTING.md is the contract. Keeping bd's state out of the
# repo means a fresh clone never inherits a tracker it cannot open: bd stores
# issues in an embedded Dolt database that is itself ignored, so the committed
# files were only ever a stale husk pointing at a database nobody else had.
.beads/
.agents/skills/beads/
.copilot-plugin/
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key

# Per-assistant config that only describes one machine's tooling. AGENTS.md is
# the brief every agent reads and is tracked; these are unfilled scaffolds that
# duplicate it, and CLAUDE.md still carries the beads block whose database is
# ignored above — committing it would hand a clone a tracker it cannot open.
.claude/
.codex/
CLAUDE.md

# Local presentation artwork. The deck ships original artwork (docs/deck/
# poster.svg) because this repository is MIT-licensed and cannot redistribute
# a film's own poster. Presenting is not publishing, so index.html will pick up
# a poster.local.<ext> placed beside it — ignored here so that a licensed or
# personal image used on stage can never be committed by accident. Git makes
# that mistake expensive: a pushed blob stays fetchable at its old SHA even
# after a later commit removes the file.
docs/deck/poster.local.*
